    fix(resolution): drop the bin-root dependency guard now that #765 placement is rustc's (#749)
    
    #765 places `#[path]` modules as rustc does, so the placement half of `bin_dep_guard`
    (misplaced-mount files) is gone with the machinery it read, and the five rows that
    bound the decoy through re-exports, third-crate re-exports and typed receivers are
    un-ignored and pass (W2a, W2b, R1, R2, R3). C17/C17b/C17d now assert rustc's file.
    The block-scope shadow refusal (review W1, #768) is not made redundant by #765 and
    stays: `bin_dep_guard.rs` keeps only that check (`ScopeGraph::bin_dep_entries`). Lane:
    the two placement mutants are removed and the three shadow mutants re-anchored.
    CPG cache stays at the 165 of the rebased cache commit.
    
